  // ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ talking (dialogue.ts)
  'quest.cargo.offer': 'Quest — The Steel Cargo: Tam\'s crate of Wyrmsteel for Bram is held by the watch. Get Sergeant Hale\'s release, then haul it to the forge: Bram could temper your blade with it.',
  'recruit.orla.intro': 'Orla Brask, Tam\'s cousin, fights for the docks\' pride. She is looking for comrades for the team bouts to come.',
  'line.mara.shut': '« My stall is shut, love. Come back with the sun. »',
  'line.mara.shortage': '« Blades cost four tenths more since the forge burned: {cause}. I don\'t like it either. »',
  'line.mara.wares': '« Whetstones, salves, a good imported blade. Everything a fighter needs, and no questions. »',
  'line.mara.lampOil': '« A man in a hood bought all my lamp oil and a pot of pitch. He asked when the smith sleeps. I didn\'t like his eyes. »',
  'line.mara.trade': '« The tournament crowds are good for trade. The ribbons sold out by noon. »',
  'line.mara.discount': '« For you, a tenth off. You carried my crates. »',
  'line.bram.repaired': '« New bellows, and Orla\'s back to thank for half of it. The fire\'s good again. »',
  'line.bram.delivered': '« The Wyrmsteel came! Give me a slot and ten coins and your blade will sing. »',
  'line.bram.done': '« Mind that edge. It\'ll cut through Marek\'s guard if anything does. »',
  'line.bram.waiting': '« My Wyrmsteel is stuck at the watch-house. Tam was to fetch it. Without it I can only sharpen what you have. »',
  'line.hale.quiet': '« The quay is quiet. My men are on every corner. »',
  'line.hale.thin': '« We\'re stretched thin, with the crowds. If something happens tonight, I\'ll hear of it too late. »',
  'line.hale.cargo': '« Tam\'s crate? Wyrmsteel for Bram. I can sign the release. »',
  'line.hale.forge': '« The forge... If you learn who paid for that, bring me a name. »',
  'line.hale.night': '« Fifteen coins and two of my men stand by Bram\'s forge till dawn. »',
  'line.wynn.loiterer': '« There\'s a hooded one who paces round the forge at dusk. I\'d not leave it alone tonight. »',
  'line.wynn.caught': '« We caught him with the pitch pot in his hands! Thanks to you, {name}. »',
  'line.wynn.night': '« Long night. The tournament makes the quay jumpy. »',
  'line.wynn.day': '« Move along, fighter. Or don\'t: it\'s a free quay. »',
  'line.stranger.day': 'The hooded figure turns away: « Not in daylight. »',
  'line.stranger.fire': '« Ten coins, and I tell you who paid for the fire. »',
  'line.stranger.whisper': '« Ten coins buy a whisper. Whispers keep fighters alive. »',
  'line.tam.asked': '« Hale has the crate under seal. Get his release, and we haul it together. »',
  'line.tam.papers': '« You got the papers! Let\'s roll it to Bram before someone else gets ideas. »',
  'line.tam.done': '« My cousin Orla says you hauled like a docker. From her, that\'s love. »',
  'line.tam.offer': '« You\'re in the pool? My cousin Orla too. Say, you look strong: I\'ve a crate of Wyrmsteel for Bram stuck at the watch-house... »',
  'line.folk.won': '« That\'s {name}! I saw you on the sand! »',
  'line.folk.lost': '« Hard luck in the arena, {name}. The pool isn\'t over. »',
  'line.folk.roar': '« The whole Cité is at the Colosseum. Listen to them roar! »',
  'line.folk.heralds': '« The heralds say the pool of eight is the strongest in years. »',
  'line.folk.forge': '« Did you hear? Bram\'s forge burned in the night. Some say it was no accident. »',
  'line.folk.feud': '« House Dree\'s men and the Temple\'s wardens nearly came to blows by the bridge. »',
  'line.folk.danger': '« People say someone powerful wants a fighter of the pool to fall. »',
  'line.odo.signed': '« You are on the roll. Bouts at the afternoon bell, days two and three. A defeat costs points, not your place. »',
  'line.odo.sign': '« A fighter for the pool? Sign here. Eight names, two rounds before the first cut. »',
  'line.anwen.hurt': '« Sit. That wound will cost you in the arena if you leave it. »',
  'line.anwen.well': '« Whole and well. Keep it that way. »',
  'line.anwen.free': '« Ilse Morrow gave her purse to the Temple: no fighter pays today. »',
  'line.orla.recruit': '« When the pool turns to teams, I\'ll stand with you. The docks remember friends. »',
  'line.orla.friend': '« Tam told me about the crate. You\'re alright. Want to spar? »',
  'line.orla.meet': '« Another fighter. Can you take a hit? Let\'s find out on the practice sand. »',
  'line.vessa.lost': '« A lucky cut. Next year, I\'ll have you. »',
  'line.vessa.won': '« Don\'t take it hard. Three cuts before you see the first: nobody sees them. »',
  'line.vessa.before': '« So you\'re my first bout, {name}? Try to keep up. »',
  'line.marek.lost': '« ... Well struck. The title is not mine yet, nor yours. We will meet again. »',
  'line.marek.won': '« You lasted. Rest, and come back stronger. »',
  'line.marek.watched': '« I watched your first bout. You are patient. Good. »',
  'line.marek.before': '« I wait. When you tire, I end it. That is all there is to me. »',
  'line.cassius.prove': '« Prove it. ... You can\'t? Then smile, peasant, and drink. »',
  'line.cassius.hostile': '« {name}. The crowd\'s new pet. Enjoy it while it lasts. »',
  'line.cassius.salute': '« Ah, one of the pool\'s fillers. House Dree salutes you. »',
  'line.lio.talk': '« Ale, a bench, and the tavern\'s talk: {rhosk} drinks with no one, {ilse} gives her winnings to the Temple, and {cassius} pays everyone\'s tab. »',

