  'v2.quest.cargo.title': 'The Steel Cargo',
  'v2.quest.cargo.offer': 'Quest — The Steel Cargo: Tam\'s crate of Wyrmsteel for Bram is held by the watch, and its barge sails at dusk on day 3. Get Sergeant Hale\'s release and haul the crate to the forge before then: Bram could temper your blade with a steel the forge does not sell. If the barge sails with it, House Dree\'s steward will buy it.',
  'v2.quest.cargo.step.papers': 'Ask Sergeant Hale for the crate\'s release (the quay)',
  'v2.quest.cargo.step.haul': 'Haul the crate to the forge with Tam (the quay, by day)',
  'v2.quest.cargo.step.temper': 'Have Bram temper your blade in the Wyrmsteel (the quay, by day, {price} coins)',
  'v2.quest.cargo.reward': 'The Wyrmsteel: Attack +{atk} on whatever blade you hold, on top of the forge\'s tiers, even the last.',
  'v2.quest.cargo.failed': 'At dusk the barge casts off with Tam\'s crate. On the quay they say House Dree\'s steward bought the Wyrmsteel for Cassius Dree\'s blade.',
  'v2.quest.herbs.title': 'Sister Anwen\'s Herbs',
  'v2.quest.herbs.offer': 'Quest — Sister Anwen\'s Herbs: the arena\'s healer has used her last river moss on the pool\'s wounds. Fenwick, the river trader on the quay at night, carries some. Bring it to her before the end of day 5 and she will brew you a draught for your next bout. If not, the Temple keeps her stores for its own fighter.',
  'v2.quest.herbs.step.buy': 'Buy river moss from Fenwick (the quay, at night, {price} coins)',
  'v2.quest.herbs.step.brew': 'Brew the draught with Sister Anwen (the forecourt, by day)',
  'v2.quest.herbs.reward': 'A draught for your next bout or challenge: +{hp} health, once.',
  'v2.quest.herbs.failed': 'Sister Anwen sends word: without the river moss, the Temple has given her last stores to Ilse Morrow, its own fighter.',
  'v2.quest.herbs.buyLabel': 'Buy a bundle of river moss for Sister Anwen ({price} coins)',
  'v2.quest.herbs.buyLog': 'Fenwick weighs out a bundle of river moss: « For the arena\'s Sister? Then it\'s the good stuff. »',
  'v2.quest.herbs.brewLabel': 'Brew the draught with Sister Anwen (+{hp} health in your next bout)',
  'v2.quest.herbs.brewLog': 'Sister Anwen grinds the moss with you and corks a green draught: « Drink it before your next bout. It will hold you up a while longer ({hp} health). »',
  'v2.quest.herbs.night': 'Sister Anwen brews by daylight.',
  'v2.quest.treatise.title': 'Master Corvin\'s Treatise',
  'v2.quest.treatise.offer': 'Quest — Master Corvin\'s Treatise: a pupil of his pawned his book of forms, and it lies among Pip\'s trinkets on the festival square. Buy it back before the end of day 7 and he will teach you a form from it, past what drilling gives. Pip sells to anyone: a fighter of the pool is already asking.',
  'v2.quest.treatise.step.buy': 'Buy the treatise back from Pip (the festival square, afternoon or evening, {price} coins)',
  'v2.quest.treatise.step.study': 'Study a form of it with Master Corvin (the training ground, by day)',
  'v2.quest.treatise.reward': 'One of your skills a level up, past the training\'s 3 (level {cap} at most).',
  'v2.quest.treatise.failed': 'Pip has sold Master Corvin\'s treatise: Vessa Lark paid for it, and reads it between her drills.',
  'v2.quest.treatise.buyLabel': 'Buy back Master Corvin\'s treatise ({price} coins)',
  'v2.quest.treatise.buyLog': 'Pip hands over a worn book of forms: « The old master\'s? He can have it. Coin first. »',
  'v2.quest.treatise.studyLabel': 'Study {skill} in the treatise with Master Corvin (to level {level})',
  'v2.quest.treatise.studyLog': 'Master Corvin turns the pages with care and walks you through a form of {skill}: it is at level {level}.',
  'v2.quest.treatise.night': 'Master Corvin teaches by daylight.',
  'v2.quest.treatise.cap': 'The treatise takes a skill to level {cap} at most.',
  'v2.quest.sharps.title': 'Lio\'s Card Sharps',
  'v2.quest.sharps.offer': 'Quest — Lio\'s Card Sharps: card sharps by the stage fleece Lio\'s customers every night. Make them leave the festival square before the end of day 8: pay them off, or ask Sergeant Hale for a man of the watch and face them together. Lio\'s room hears everything, and he would tell you.',
  'v2.quest.sharps.step.face': 'Face the card sharps by the stage (the festival square, at night): pay them off ({price} coins), or ask Sergeant Hale for the watch first',
  'v2.quest.sharps.step.watch': 'Face the card sharps with Hale\'s watchman (the festival square, at night)',
  'v2.quest.sharps.reward': 'The eve of each of your bouts, Lio tells you your opponent\'s plan.',
