  'v2.passer.hettie.won': 'Hettie beams and ties {item} on your sleeve for {price} coins: « For luck at the gate. »',
  'v2.line.nell': '« Mending nets since dawn. These gloves have saved my fingers a hundred times; they could save yours on the sand. »',
  'v2.line.nell.gone': '« Bare hands today. The nets do not mind. »',
  'v2.line.jory': '« I carry the guilds\' letters down to the river towns. My spare boots are lighter than these, if you run as much as I do. »',
  'v2.line.jory.gone': '« One pair of boots will have to do. »',
  'v2.line.yselle': '« I sing for the arena\'s crowd at dusk. This charm was a gift from a champion who never came back. »',
  'v2.line.yselle.gone': '« The song goes on without the charm. »',
  'v2.line.garrick': '« Twenty years in the city guard. That gorget kept my throat whole; I only watch the drills now. »',
  'v2.line.garrick.gone': '« My old gorget has found a new throat. Keep it whole. »',
  'v2.line.maud': '« I keep the gallery\'s horses. These leathers are made for the saddle, but they turn a blade as well as a hoof. »',
  'v2.line.maud.gone': '« The horses never asked for that leather back. »',
  'v2.line.dov': '« Between two contracts. I carry a spare blade, imported, good steel; I would sell it to someone who can use it. »',
  'v2.line.dov.gone': '« The spare blade has gone. I hope it bites. »',
  'v2.line.hettie': '« Fresh bread for the square! I sew lucky ribbons too; every fighter needs one at the gate. »',
  'v2.line.hettie.gone': '« Wear my ribbon well. »',
